{
 "format": "openchronology",
 "version": 1,
 "title": "Ancient Egypt: from Narmer to Cleopatra",
 "description": "Ancient Egypt from its Predynastic cultures and its unification under Narmer to the death of Cleopatra VII and the Roman annexation in 30 BCE: its periods, dynasties and major reigns, its monuments, battles and treaties, and the writings we know it from. A sample timeline built from the sources cited on each moment.\n\n**How to read it.** Chapter headings mark the periods. Periods, dynasties and reigns are bands (navy, grey and ochre); everything else is a moment, linked to the Wikipedia article it draws on. Related things (a king and his monument, a battle and the treaty after it) are linked.\n\n**Dates.** Periods, dynasties and reigns follow one standard chronology, Ian Shaw (ed.), *The Oxford History of Ancient Egypt* (2000). Before 664 BCE every date is approximate, and other chronologies differ by years to decades; each moment's **Date precision** says how it is dated. A date known only to its year is placed on 1 January of that year. The few dates known to the day are Roman (Julian) dates, kept as given under **Historical dates**; the timeline's Gregorian display shows the same days a few dates earlier, as the two calendars differ by that much in antiquity.",
 "presentation": {
  "mode": "gregorian",
  "unit": "",
  "scale": "1/1",
  "origin": "0/1",
  "version": 1,
  "offsetMinutes": 0,
  "significantDigits": 6
 },
 "tags": [
  "history",
  "ancient egypt",
  "antiquity",
  "education"
 ],
 "plugins": [
  {
   "manifest": {
    "apiVersion": 1,
    "id": "rich-text-notes",
    "version": 1,
    "name": "Rich text notes",
    "description": "Edit moment and stack notes visually, storing portable Markdown. Hover cards render safe headings, emphasis, lists, code and HTTPS links. HTML and images are not executed.",
    "fields": [],
    "notes": {
     "kind": "markdown"
    },
    "source": "function render(moment: string, api: PluginAPI): string { return api.none(); }"
   },
   "enabled": true
  },
  {
   "manifest": {
    "apiVersion": 1,
    "id": "moment-headings",
    "version": 1,
    "name": "Headings",
    "description": "Let a moment act as a heading or marker: only its title shows, sized as a heading from level 1 to 6, and the title is what you click. Choose its font (Times New Roman by default). Headings still group into summaries with other moments.",
    "fields": [
     {
      "kind": "heading",
      "metadataKey": "headingLevel",
      "label": "Heading level"
     },
     {
      "kind": "font",
      "metadataKey": "headingFont",
      "label": "Heading font"
     }
    ],
    "marker": {
     "kind": "heading",
     "metadataKey": "headingLevel"
    },
    "targets": [
     "moments"
    ]
   },
   "enabled": true
  },
  {
   "manifest": {
    "apiVersion": 1,
    "id": "moment-colors",
    "version": 2,
    "name": "Moment colors",
    "description": "Choose muted semantic swatches or a custom color for moments and stack entries while preserving their white borders.",
    "fields": [
     {
      "kind": "color",
      "metadataKey": "color",
      "label": "Moment color"
     }
    ],
    "marker": {
     "kind": "color",
     "metadataKey": "color"
    },
    "source": "function render(moment: string, api: PluginAPI): string { return api.color(api.get(\"color\")); }"
   },
   "enabled": true
  },
  {
   "manifest": {
    "apiVersion": 1,
    "id": "moment-sources",
    "version": 1,
    "name": "Sources",
    "description": "Show and edit a series of source links for moments and stack entries.",
    "fields": [
     {
      "kind": "links",
      "metadataKey": "sources",
      "label": "Sources"
     }
    ],
    "source": "function render(moment: string, api: PluginAPI): string { return api.none(); }"
   },
   "enabled": true
  },
  {
   "manifest": {
    "apiVersion": 1,
    "id": "dating-context",
    "version": 1,
    "name": "Dating context",
    "description": "Explain the precision and coordinate convention of a moment. An exact stored coordinate can still represent an approximate age or a calendar-day marker.",
    "fields": [
     {
      "kind": "text",
      "metadataKey": "datePrecision",
      "label": "Date precision"
     },
     {
      "kind": "multiline",
      "metadataKey": "coordinateConvention",
      "label": "Coordinate convention"
     }
    ],
    "source": "function render(moment: string, api: PluginAPI): string { return api.none(); }"
   },
   "enabled": true
  },
  {
   "manifest": {
    "apiVersion": 1,
    "id": "historical-dates",
    "version": 1,
    "name": "Historical dates",
    "description": "Retain an original historical date and its calendar separately from the timeline coordinate and display calendar, such as a Julian date on a Gregorian timeline.",
    "fields": [
     {
      "kind": "text",
      "metadataKey": "historicalDate",
      "label": "Original historical date"
     },
     {
      "kind": "text",
      "metadataKey": "calendar",
      "label": "Original calendar"
     }
    ],
    "source": "function render(moment: string, api: PluginAPI): string { return api.none(); }"
   },
   "enabled": true
  },
  {
   "manifest": {
    "apiVersion": 1,
    "id": "expand-on-hover",
    "version": 1,
    "name": "Expand on hover",
    "description": "Hover or focus a summary of two to five moments to fan out its members radially for individual inspection. Larger summaries stay collapsed.",
    "fields": [],
    "summary": {
     "kind": "radial"
    },
    "source": "function render(moment: string, api: PluginAPI): string { return api.expand(); }"
   },
   "enabled": true
  },
  {
   "manifest": {
    "apiVersion": 1,
    "id": "timeline-theme",
    "version": 2,
    "name": "Timeline theme",
    "description": "Choose the timeline's colors, fonts and text sizes: its labels, its measure (the axis, tick marks and their times), the halo that keeps them readable over images, the default marker and duration colors, and a background color. Set them here in the plugin list; anything left blank keeps the usual look, and colors chosen for events still win.",
    "fields": [],
    "settings": [
     {
      "kind": "color",
      "key": "textColor",
      "label": "Label color"
     },
     {
      "kind": "font",
      "key": "textFont",
      "label": "Label font"
     },
     {
      "kind": "text-size",
      "key": "textSize",
      "label": "Label size"
     },
     {
      "kind": "color",
      "key": "measureColor",
      "label": "Measure color"
     },
     {
      "kind": "font",
      "key": "measureFont",
      "label": "Measure font"
     },
     {
      "kind": "text-size",
      "key": "measureSize",
      "label": "Measure size"
     },
     {
      "kind": "color",
      "key": "haloColor",
      "label": "Halo color"
     },
     {
      "kind": "color",
      "key": "markerColor",
      "label": "Marker color"
     },
     {
      "kind": "color",
      "key": "durationColor",
      "label": "Duration color"
     },
     {
      "kind": "color",
      "key": "backgroundColor",
      "label": "Background color"
     }
    ],
    "theme": {
     "text": "textColor",
     "textFont": "textFont",
     "textSize": "textSize",
     "measure": "measureColor",
     "measureFont": "measureFont",
     "measureSize": "measureSize",
     "halo": "haloColor",
     "marker": "markerColor",
     "duration": "durationColor",
     "background": "backgroundColor"
    }
   },
   "enabled": true,
   "settings": {
    "textColor": "#1f2a44",
    "textFont": "Georgia, serif",
    "measureColor": "#9c3b2a",
    "haloColor": "#f3ead7",
    "markerColor": "#1f3a5f",
    "durationColor": "#9c3b2a",
    "backgroundColor": "#f3ead7"
   }
  }
 ],
 "events": [
  {
   "id": "h-predynastic",
   "time": "-200986185600/1",
   "metadata": {
    "title": "Predynastic Egypt",
    "tags": [
     "chapter"
    ],
    "headingLevel": "h2",
    "datePrecision": "About 4400 BCE, in Shaw's chronology (Oxford History of Ancient Egypt, 2000); other chronologies differ."
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "hierakonpolis",
   "time": "-172584950400/1",
   "metadata": {
    "title": "Painted tomb at Hierakonpolis",
    "description": "**Tomb 100** at **Hierakonpolis**, the oldest known painted tomb in Egypt, shows boats, hunters and a figure subduing captives: themes of kingship long before there were kings of all Egypt.",
    "tags": [
     "monument"
    ],
    "sources": [
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hierakonpolis"
    ],
    "datePrecision": "About 3500 BCE, in Shaw's chronology (Oxford History of Ancient Egypt, 2000); other chronologies differ. Naqada II."
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "u-j",
   "time": "-164695766400/1",
   "metadata": {
    "title": "Tomb U-j: the earliest writing",
    "description": "Small bone and ivory labels from **tomb U-j** at **Abydos** carry some of the oldest known signs of Egyptian writing, recording places and goods.",
    "tags": [
     "writing"
    ],
    "sources": [
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Umm_El_Qa%27ab",
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Egyptian_hieroglyphs"
    ],
    "datePrecision": "About 3250 BCE (Naqada IIIA), from radiocarbon dates; c. 3320–3150 BCE."
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "h-early",
   "time": "-156806496000/1",
   "metadata": {
    "title": "Early Dynastic Period",
    "tags": [
     "chapter"
    ],
    "headingLevel": "h2",
    "datePrecision": "About 3000 BCE, in Shaw's chronology (Oxford History of Ancient Egypt, 2000); other chronologies differ."
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "unification",
   "time": "-156806496000/1",
   "metadata": {
    "title": "Unification under Narmer",
    "description": "**Narmer** is the first king known to have ruled both Upper and Lower Egypt, and is usually counted the founder of the **1st Dynasty**. Later tradition credits a king **Menes** with the union.",
    "tags": [
     "ruler",
     "war"
    ],
    "sources": [
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Narmer",
     "https://academic.oup.com/book/47196"
    ],
    "datePrecision": "About 3000 BCE, in Shaw's chronology (Oxford History of Ancient Egypt, 2000); other chronologies differ. Many works put Narmer nearer 3100 BCE."
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "narmer-palette",
   "time": "-156806496000/1",
   "metadata": {
    "title": "Narmer Palette",
    "description": "A carved siltstone palette from **Hierakonpolis** showing **Narmer** wearing the crown of Upper Egypt on one side and of Lower Egypt on the other, his name written in early hieroglyphs. Now in the **Egyptian Museum, Cairo**.",
    "tags": [
     "writing",
     "monument"
    ],
    "sources": [
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Narmer_Palette"
    ],
    "datePrecision": "About 3000 BCE, in Shaw's chronology (Oxford History of Ancient Egypt, 2000); other chronologies differ."
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "memphis",
   "time": "-156490963200/1",
   "metadata": {
    "title": "Memphis founded",
    "description": "**Memphis**, at the meeting of the Nile valley and the Delta, became the capital of the united kingdom. Herodotus credits its founding to **Menes**.",
    "tags": [
     "monument"
    ],
    "sources": [
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Memphis,_Egypt"
    ],
    "datePrecision": "About 3000 BCE, in Shaw's chronology (Oxford History of Ancient Egypt, 2000); other chronologies differ. Early in the 1st Dynasty; placed just after the unification."
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "h-old",
   "time": "-146897625600/1",
   "metadata": {
    "title": "Old Kingdom",
    "tags": [
     "chapter"
    ],
    "headingLevel": "h2",
    "datePrecision": "About 2686 BCE, in Shaw's chronology (Oxford History of Ancient Egypt, 2000); other chronologies differ."
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "step-pyramid",
   "time": "-146298009600/1",
   "metadata": {
    "title": "Step Pyramid of Djoser",
    "description": "At **Saqqara**, **Djoser**'s official **Imhotep** is credited with the first monumental building in stone: six stacked mastabas, the earliest Egyptian pyramid.",
    "tags": [
     "monument"
    ],
    "sources": [
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pyramid_of_Djoser",
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Imhotep"
    ],
    "datePrecision": "About 2667 BCE, in Shaw's chronology (Oxford History of Ancient Egypt, 2000); other chronologies differ. Built during Djoser's reign (2667–2648 BCE); placed at its start."
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "dahshur",
   "time": "-144183715200/1",
   "metadata": {
    "title": "Sneferu's pyramids at Dahshur",
    "description": "**Sneferu** builds the **Bent Pyramid**, whose slope changes halfway up, and then the **Red Pyramid**, the first successful smooth-sided pyramid.",
    "tags": [
     "monument"
    ],
    "sources": [
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bent_Pyramid",
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red_Pyramid"
    ],
    "datePrecision": "About 2600 BCE, in Shaw's chronology (Oxford History of Ancient Egypt, 2000); other chronologies differ. During Sneferu's reign (2613–2589 BCE)."
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "merer",
   "time": "-143142336000/1",
   "metadata": {
    "title": "Diary of Merer",
    "description": "Papyri found at **Wadi al-Jarf** on the Red Sea, the oldest inscribed papyri known, include the logbook of an official named **Merer** whose crew shipped limestone from Tura to **Giza** for the Great Pyramid.",
    "tags": [
     "writing",
     "monument"
    ],
    "sources": [
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diary_of_Merer"
    ],
    "datePrecision": "Dated to about Khufu's 27th year: later than his reign ends in Shaw's chronology (2589–2566 BCE), a sign of how uncertain reign lengths are. Placed near the end of the reign."
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "great-pyramid",
   "time": "-143110800000/1",
   "metadata": {
    "title": "Great Pyramid of Giza",
    "description": "**Khufu**'s pyramid at **Giza**, about 146 m high when finished, the largest of the pyramids and the oldest of the Seven Wonders of the Ancient World.",
    "tags": [
     "monument"
    ],
    "sources": [
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Great_Pyramid_of_Giza"
    ],
    "datePrecision": "About 2566 BCE, in Shaw's chronology (Oxford History of Ancient Egypt, 2000); other chronologies differ. Finished by the end of Khufu's reign; often given as c. 2560 BCE."
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "sphinx",
   "time": "-142605878400/1",
   "metadata": {
    "title": "Great Sphinx of Giza",
    "description": "A lion with a king's head carved from the bedrock beside the causeway of **Khafra**'s pyramid, and usually attributed to him.",
    "tags": [
     "monument"
    ],
    "sources": [
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Great_Sphinx_of_Giza"
    ],
    "datePrecision": "About 2550 BCE, in Shaw's chronology (Oxford History of Ancient Egypt, 2000); other chronologies differ. During Khafra's reign (2558–2532 BCE), on the usual attribution."
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "palermo-stone",
   "time": "-139450204800/1",
   "metadata": {
    "title": "Palermo Stone",
    "description": "Fragments of a royal annal carved in the **5th Dynasty**, listing kings from before the 1st Dynasty to **Neferirkara**, with events and the Nile flood year by year: one of the oldest sources for the order of the kings.",
    "tags": [
     "writing"
    ],
    "sources": [
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Palermo_Stone"
    ],
    "datePrecision": "About 2450 BCE, in Shaw's chronology (Oxford History of Ancient Egypt, 2000); other chronologies differ. Carved in the 5th Dynasty (2494–2345 BCE)."
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "pyramid-texts",
   "time": "-136294444800/1",
   "metadata": {
    "title": "Pyramid Texts",
    "description": "Spells to help the king join the gods, carved on the walls of **Unas**'s pyramid at **Saqqara**: the oldest religious texts known from Egypt.",
    "tags": [
     "writing",
     "monument"
    ],
    "sources": [
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pyramid_Texts"
    ],
    "datePrecision": "About 2350 BCE, in Shaw's chronology (Oxford History of Ancient Egypt, 2000); other chronologies differ. During Unas's reign (2375–2345 BCE)."
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "harkhuf",
   "time": "-133990848000/1",
   "metadata": {
    "title": "Harkhuf's letter from the boy king",
    "description": "The expedition leader **Harkhuf** had carved in his tomb at **Aswan** a letter from the young **Pepi II**, eager to see a dancer Harkhuf was bringing back from the land of **Yam**.",
    "tags": [
     "writing",
     "diplomacy"
    ],
    "sources": [
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Harkhuf"
    ],
    "datePrecision": "About 2277 BCE, in Shaw's chronology (Oxford History of Ancient Egypt, 2000); other chronologies differ. In Pepi II's second year."
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "drought",
   "time": "-131560934400/1",
   "metadata": {
    "title": "The 4.2-kiloyear drought",
    "description": "A severe, centuries-long drying across North Africa and western Asia, with low Nile floods, often linked to the end of central rule at the close of the **Old Kingdom**.",
    "tags": [
     "science"
    ],
    "sources": [
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/4.2-kiloyear_event"
    ],
    "datePrecision": "About 2200 BCE (4,200 years before 2000 CE); a climatic event dated by geology."
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "h-first-intermediate",
   "time": "-130298630400/1",
   "metadata": {
    "title": "First Intermediate Period",
    "tags": [
     "chapter"
    ],
    "headingLevel": "h2",
    "datePrecision": "About 2160 BCE, in Shaw's chronology (Oxford History of Ancient Egypt, 2000); other chronologies differ."
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "coffin-texts",
   "time": "-128405260800/1",
   "metadata": {
    "title": "Coffin Texts",
    "description": "Spells descended from the **Pyramid Texts**, now painted inside the coffins of officials and their families, not only kings.",
    "tags": [
     "writing"
    ],
    "sources": [
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coffin_Texts"
    ],
    "datePrecision": "About 2100 BCE, in Shaw's chronology (Oxford History of Ancient Egypt, 2000); other chronologies differ. In use from the First Intermediate Period into the Middle Kingdom."
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "reunification",
   "time": "-126038505600/1",
   "metadata": {
    "title": "Thebes reunites Egypt",
    "description": "**Mentuhotep II** of **Thebes** defeats the rival kings of **Herakleopolis** and rules the whole country again.",
    "tags": [
     "war",
     "ruler"
    ],
    "sources": [
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mentuhotep_II"
    ],
    "datePrecision": "About 2025 BCE, in Shaw's chronology (Oxford History of Ancient Egypt, 2000); other chronologies differ. The end of the Herakleopolitan dynasties in Shaw's dates; Mentuhotep II reigned 2055–2004 BCE."
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "h-middle",
   "time": "-126985190400/1",
   "metadata": {
    "title": "Middle Kingdom",
    "tags": [
     "chapter"
    ],
    "headingLevel": "h2",
    "datePrecision": "About 2055 BCE, in Shaw's chronology (Oxford History of Ancient Egypt, 2000); other chronologies differ."
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "itjtawy",
   "time": "-124776201600/1",
   "metadata": {
    "title": "Itjtawy, the new capital",
    "description": "**Amenemhat I**, founder of the **12th Dynasty**, moves the royal residence north to **Itjtawy**, near the Faiyum.",
    "tags": [
     "monument",
     "ruler"
    ],
    "sources": [
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Itjtawy"
    ],
    "datePrecision": "About 1985 BCE, in Shaw's chronology (Oxford History of Ancient Egypt, 2000); other chronologies differ. Early in his reign (1985–1956 BCE)."
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "sinuhe",
   "time": "-123671664000/1",
   "metadata": {
    "title": "The Story of Sinuhe",
    "description": "A courtier flees Egypt when **Amenemhat I** dies, makes a life in Syria-Palestine, and is welcomed home in old age by **Senusret I**: the most admired work of Middle Egyptian literature.",
    "tags": [
     "writing"
    ],
    "sources": [
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Story_of_Sinuhe"
    ],
    "datePrecision": "About 1950 BCE, in Shaw's chronology (Oxford History of Ancient Egypt, 2000); other chronologies differ. Written in the 12th Dynasty, probably early in Senusret I’s reign (1956–1911 BCE)."
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "karnak",
   "time": "-123513897600/1",
   "metadata": {
    "title": "Karnak: the temple of Amun",
    "description": "**Senusret I** builds at **Karnak**, in Thebes; later kings, above all in the New Kingdom, enlarge it into the largest temple complex of ancient Egypt.",
    "tags": [
     "monument"
    ],
    "sources": [
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Karnak"
    ],
    "datePrecision": "About 1945 BCE, in Shaw's chronology (Oxford History of Ancient Egypt, 2000); other chronologies differ. Senusret I's buildings are the oldest standing there."
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "semna",
   "time": "-120673756800/1",
   "metadata": {
    "title": "Semna boundary stela",
    "description": "**Senusret III**, after his campaigns in Nubia, sets a stela at the fortress of **Semna** marking the southern frontier and urging his successors to hold it.",
    "tags": [
     "war",
     "writing"
    ],
    "sources": [
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Senusret_III"
    ],
    "datePrecision": "About 1855 BCE, in Shaw's chronology (Oxford History of Ancient Egypt, 2000); other chronologies differ. In Senusret III's 16th year."
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "h-second-intermediate",
   "time": "-114204643200/1",
   "metadata": {
    "title": "Second Intermediate Period",
    "tags": [
     "chapter"
    ],
    "headingLevel": "h2",
    "datePrecision": "About 1650 BCE, in Shaw's chronology (Oxford History of Ancient Egypt, 2000); other chronologies differ."
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "hyksos",
   "time": "-114204643200/1",
   "metadata": {
    "title": "The Hyksos rule from Avaris",
    "description": "Kings of western Asian origin, the **Hyksos** (\"rulers of foreign lands\"), govern the north from **Avaris** in the eastern Delta as the **15th Dynasty**, while Theban kings hold the south.",
    "tags": [
     "ruler",
     "war"
    ],
    "sources": [
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hyksos"
    ],
    "datePrecision": "About 1650 BCE, in Shaw's chronology (Oxford History of Ancient Egypt, 2000); other chronologies differ."
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "edwin-smith",
   "time": "-112626720000/1",
   "metadata": {
    "title": "Edwin Smith Papyrus",
    "description": "A surgical treatise: 48 cases of wounds and fractures, each examined, diagnosed and treated in order. A copy of an older text.",
    "tags": [
     "writing",
     "science"
    ],
    "sources": [
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Edwin_Smith_Papyrus"
    ],
    "datePrecision": "About 1600 BCE, from its script; a copy of a text perhaps centuries older."
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "seqenenre",
   "time": "-111364416000/1",
   "metadata": {
    "title": "Seqenenra Taa killed",
    "description": "The Theban king **Seqenenra Taa**'s mummy shows the axe and dagger wounds that killed him, probably in battle against the **Hyksos**.",
    "tags": [
     "war",
     "ruler"
    ],
    "sources": [
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seqenenre_Tao"
    ],
    "datePrecision": "About 1560 BCE, in Shaw's chronology (Oxford History of Ancient Egypt, 2000); other chronologies differ."
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "kamose",
   "time": "-111206649600/1",
   "metadata": {
    "title": "Kamose attacks the Hyksos",
